  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and seasonable today, but summer heat and \nhumidity returns Wed through the weekend. Diurnal scattered \nthunderstorms possible each day.\n\nA weak high pressure builds in today in the wake of a cold \nfront, bringing clearing skies and dry weather with high \ntemperatures in the low to mid 80s. Dew points begin to surge \ninto the mid 70s Wednesday, peaking Thursday and Friday, and \nlinger into the weekend as a Bermuda high builds in across the \nwestern Atlantic Ocean. Prolonged southerly flow will advect \nthose warmer dew points into southern New England through the \nsecond half of the week, leading to near oppressive humidity at \ntimes. 925mb temperatures surge to near +22C each afternoon \nthis week, leading to high temps 85-90 every day. Combined with \ndew points of 72-76, heat headlines are being considered through\nthe second half of the week and possibly into the weekend.\n\nRegarding the thunderstorm potential later in the week... a few\nweak, upper level disturbances passing through New England \ncombining with the high heat/humidity and just enough \ninstability will likely be enough to pop a few diurnal \nshowers/thunderstorms each day Thursday through the weekend. \nPWATs anywhere from 1.75\" to 2.10\" will also provide enough \npotential for storms to be water loaded with torrential \ndownpours.",
